.TH INKWELL 1 "" "Inkwell" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inkwell \- collaborative Typst and Markdown editor, without a server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inkwell
.br
.B inkwell
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Inkwell
opens a window to write Typst or Markdown documents, alone or with other people.
People who write together are connected directly to each other; there is no account
and no server. Each person keeps a full copy of the project on their computer, edits
continue offline, and they are merged when people meet again.
.PP
Inkwell takes no file argument: it opens the most recent project of the Inkwell folder
in the Documents folder of the user, and creates one on first launch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version (SemVer), the commit and the build date, then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INKWELL_DOCS
Folder that holds the projects, instead of
.IR Inkwell " in the Documents folder."
.TP
.B INKWELL_HOME
Folder that holds the identity of the user (the keys), instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/inkwell .
.TP
.B INKWELL_LAN
Set to
.B 1
to find other people on the local network.
.TP
.B INKWELL_RENDEZVOUS
URL of the server that carries the short invitation codes; the word
.B off
turns the codes off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Documents/Inkwell/
The projects. Their files are ordinary files; uninstalling Inkwell never touches them.
.TP
.I ~/.config/inkwell/
The identity of the user.
.SH SEE ALSO
Typst, https://typst.app/docs/
.PP
Project home page, https://github.com/oioio-space/inkwell
